-- title:
--   Places of the reduced modular field agreeing on the finite chart
-- statement:
--   Let $N\ge 1$, let $\ell$ be a prime, let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, let $k$ be a field of characteristic $\ell$ and let $\mathrm{red}\colon A\to k$ be a surjective ring homomorphism. Let $fm$ be a fibre model of level $N$ for these data; its finite chart is a subring $fm.\mathrm{BFin}$ of $\mathrm{laurentBaseChange}\,\overline{\mathbb{Q}}\,(\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldFull}\ N)$, the subfield of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$ generated over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ by the coefficientwise image of the full level-$N$ modular function field over $\mathbb{Q}$, containing the constants from $A$ and the elements $\mathrm{jBar}$, $\mathrm{jNBar}$, integral over the subring generated by the constants and $\mathrm{jBar}$, and equipped with a ring homomorphism $fm.\mathrm{piFin}$ into $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N=k(\mathrm{jqModC}\,k,\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N)\subseteq k((q))$ reducing constants via $\mathrm{red}$ and sending $\mathrm{jBar},\mathrm{jNBar}$ to $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k,\mathrm{jqNModC}\,k\,N$. Assume given, for every positive $d\mid N$, modular polynomial data for level $d$ (a monic $\Phi_d\in\mathbb{Z}[X][Y]$ of degree $\psi(d)$ in $Y$ vanishing at $(j(q),j(q^d))$), and assume that $\Phi_N$, with coefficients reduced into $k$ and read in $\mathrm{RatFunc}\,k[Y]$, is separable. Let $v_1,v_2$ be places of $\mathrm{modularFunctionFieldC}\ k\ N$, that is, valuation subrings containing $k$, proper, and principal ideal rings, and suppose $\mathrm{jqModC}\,k$ lies in the valuation ring of each. If for every $b\in fm.\mathrm{BFin}$ the element $fm.\mathrm{piFin}(b)$ lies in the maximal ideal of $v_1$ exactly when it lies in the maximal ideal of $v_2$, then $v_1=v_2$.
--
--   This is the finite-chart extensionality principle for places of the reduced modular function field: a place at which $j$ is regular is determined by its centre on the finite chart ring. It is used in the computation of the specialisation map on places and of the associated order functions, for instance in [`ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.mapDomain_spPlace_eq_ord_coeffMap`](thm.html#ModularCurve.CharPModel.FibreModel.mapDomain_spPlace_eq_ord_coeffMap) and in the treatment of Hecke divisors.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_ModularCurve_CharPModel_FibreModel_place_eq_of_forall_finChart_mem_nonunits_iff.lean

import Definitions.Def_ModularCurve_SpecializationMap

set_option maxHeartbeats 4000000
